'' An array argument chooses an overload by its rank -- the one it was declared with, or,
'' for 'dim a( )', the one its first redim gave it. fbc-modern 1.20 runs the source and
'' prints 1 2 1 2, and so does a tiko-lang build of it (2026-09-18); before, all four
'' calls were TKO0660, ambiguous. Each call is asserted with its argument.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/symbols/src/overload-by-rank.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: error TKO
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1FR8FBARRAY1Iu7INTEGERE(@array1)
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1FR8FBARRAY2Iu7INTEGERE(@array2)
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1FR8FBARRAY1Iu7INTEGERE(@byredim1)
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Z1FR8FBARRAY2Iu7INTEGERE(@byredim2)
